flowchart TB
    accTitle: Notifications about new documents
    accDescr: Every five minutes, a background job asks Paperless-ngx once for the documents that it added since the last run, and they wait for their files. While no file has arrived, Paperless gets no further request. Once a file is in the archive account, the job asks Paperless once per distinct saved search which of those documents it finds. Each user who asked for a document and can open its file gets one notification, with a link to each file that it names.

    job["Every five minutes,<br>the background job"]
    paperless[("Paperless-ngx: one request<br>for the documents added since the last run")]
    waiting{"Has the file of a waiting document<br>reached the archive account?"}
    rest["No further request:<br>the document waits, up to two days"]
    searches[("Paperless-ngx: one request<br>per distinct saved search,<br>among those documents alone")]
    files["For each user who asked:<br>the files of the archive account<br>that the user can open"]
    notification(["`**One notification for jamie**
    2 new documents in Paperless
    *each title opens its file*`"])

    job --> paperless
    paperless --> waiting
    waiting -- "no" --> rest
    waiting -- "yes" --> searches
    searches --> files
    files --> notification

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef app fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef yes fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class job you
    class waiting,rest,files app
    class notification yes
